  "build_note": "Source-built from the pinned sdist with clang 14 -O0 and LLVM source coverage on every translation unit (pybind11 2.13.6 and setuptools 80.9.0 as build backend, pinned by hash). PyPI publishes no linux/aarch64 wheel for 1.1.0; the official x86_64 wheels build the same sources without coverage instrumentation.",
  "dependencies_note": "pytomlpp has no Python runtime dependencies; pybind11 is a build-time header library. The toml++ parser is vendored in the sdist, not fetched separately.",
  "parser_family": "toml++ (marzer/tomlplusplus), C++: pytomlpp's pybind11 _impl.loads calls toml::parse(std::string_view) from the toml++ headers vendored in the sdist (a submodule snapshot after the v3.4.0 tag; 17 of 49 impl headers differ from v3.4.0, mostly portability macros, with 26 changed lines in the 3,917-line parser.inl) and converts the toml::table with its own type casters. Same parser family as the selected C++ toml++ 3.4.0 path; independent of tomli/tomllib, tomlkit and the Rust toml_parser family of rtoml.",
